---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import portraitTall from '../../assets/images/preview/gathering.jpg';
import band from '../../assets/images/preview/c-band.jpg';
import inset from '../../assets/images/preview/c-inset.jpg';
---

<Layout
	title="Creative Work placements"
	noindex
	description="Mock-up route: three placements for the reading photograph on the Creative Work page."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="mock-head">
			<p class="mock-kicker">Mock-up &mdash; not linked from the site</p>
			<h1>Where the reading photograph goes</h1>
			<p class="mock-intro">
				Three placements for candidate&nbsp;C on Creative Work, each shown in the
				real page. The prose is abridged after the first two paragraphs of{' '}
				<em>Flight</em>; everything else &mdash; measure, type, rules &mdash; is
				what the page actually renders.
			</p>
		</header>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />

	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="mock-label">1 &mdash; beside the page head</p>
		<p class="mock-note">
			The home page&rsquo;s move, repeated here. Puts you at the top of the page,
			but it narrows the intro line and makes Creative Work open on a portrait
			rather than on the work.
		</p>

		<header class="page-head split">
			<div>
				<h2 class="as-h1">Creative Work</h2>
				<p class="page-intro">A novel and published poems.</p>
			</div>
			<Image
				class="head-portrait"
				src={portraitTall}
				alt=""
				widths={[224, 336, 448]}
				sizes="(max-width: 46rem) 40vw, 12rem"
			/>
		</header>

		<section class="work">
			<h2><em>Flight</em></h2>
			<p class="work-meta">A novel &middot; 80,000 words &middot; Under agent&nbsp;review</p>
			<p>
				<em>Flight</em> is a work of literary fiction about risk and resistance,
				light and dark energies&nbsp;&mdash; and the barriers people create to
				preserve their comfortable, ziplocked lives.
			</p>
			<p class="mock-elision">[&hellip; remainder of the section &hellip;]</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />

	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="mock-label">2 &mdash; a band under the page head</p>
		<p class="mock-note">
			The shelf-band move from the home page. The photograph runs the full
			measure on its own tinted ground, so the page still opens on the words and
			the picture arrives as a beat before <em>Flight</em>.
		</p>

		<header class="page-head">
			<h2 class="as-h1">Creative Work</h2>
			<p class="page-intro">A novel and published poems.</p>
		</header>
	</div>

	<section class="photo-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<Image
				class="band-image"
				src={band}
				alt=""
				widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
				sizes="(max-width: 53rem) 92vw, 50rem"
			/>
			<p class="band-caption">Reading from the novel, 2013.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="wrap">
		<section class="work no-rule">
			<h2><em>Flight</em></h2>
			<p class="work-meta">A novel &middot; 80,000 words &middot; Under agent&nbsp;review</p>
			<p>
				<em>Flight</em> is a work of literary fiction about risk and resistance,
				light and dark energies&nbsp;&mdash; and the barriers people create to
				preserve their comfortable, ziplocked lives.
			</p>
			<p class="mock-elision">[&hellip; remainder of the section &hellip;]</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />

	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="mock-label">3 &mdash; inset beside the poems</p>
		<p class="mock-note">
			Smallest of the three. The page opens on the novel, and the photograph
			appears where it is literally true &mdash; you are reading aloud, and the
			Merton poems below were read aloud by their editor.
		</p>

		<header class="page-head">
			<h2 class="as-h1">Creative Work</h2>
			<p class="page-intro">A novel and published poems.</p>
		</header>

		<section class="work">
			<h2><em>Flight</em></h2>
			<p class="work-meta">A novel &middot; 80,000 words &middot; Under agent&nbsp;review</p>
			<p class="mock-elision">[&hellip; the section as it stands &hellip;]</p>
		</section>

		<section class="work">
			<div class="measure">
			<Image
				class="inset-image"
				src={inset}
				alt=""
				widths={[176, 264, 352]}
				sizes="(max-width: 46rem) 34vw, 11rem"
			/>
			<h2>Poems</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Trappists&rdquo; and &ldquo;Houdini.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>The Antigonish Review</em> 153 (Summer 2008): 76&ndash;79.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Retreating.&rdquo;</span>{' '}
					<em>The Merton Journal</em> 15.1 (Eastertide 2008): 12&ndash;13.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;The Shower (for Thomas&nbsp;Merton).&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					<em>The Merton Journal</em> 10.2 (Advent 2003): 13&ndash;14. Read by the
					editor at the annual meeting of the Thomas&nbsp;Merton Society of
					Great&nbsp;Britain and Ireland.
				</li>
			</ul>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />

	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="mock-label">4 &mdash; inset in the <em>Flight</em> section</p>
		<p class="mock-note">
			The same inset as 3, moved to where the prose actually is. <em>Flight</em>{' '}
			has three paragraphs for the picture to sit against; the poems are a list,
			which gives a float nothing to wrap around.
		</p>

		<header class="page-head">
			<h2 class="as-h1">Creative Work</h2>
			<p class="page-intro">A novel and published poems.</p>
		</header>

		<section class="work">
			<div class="measure">
				<Image
					class="inset-image"
					src={inset}
					alt=""
					widths={[176, 264, 352]}
					sizes="(max-width: 46rem) 34vw, 11rem"
				/>
				<h2><em>Flight</em></h2>
				<p class="work-meta">A novel &middot; 80,000 words &middot; Under agent&nbsp;review</p>
				<p>
					<em>Flight</em> is a work of literary fiction about risk and resistance,
					light and dark energies&nbsp;&mdash; and the barriers people create to
					preserve their comfortable, ziplocked lives.
				</p>
				<p>
					Structured in six sections that correspond to spiritual dates and
					martyrs, the novel dramatizes two months in the life of a woman who
					works in an exotic bird store. Her best friend is a circus
					contortionist. She has three love interests: a bashful policeman, an
					egomaniacal astrophysicist, and a distant fianc&eacute;. At the center
					of her story is Maddie, a yellow-collared macaw.
				</p>
				<p>
					It is perhaps the most meaningful project I have completed.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />

	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="mock-label">5 &mdash; a column beside <em>Flight</em>, not a float</p>
		<p class="mock-note">
			Same idea, built as a grid instead. The prose keeps one measure the whole
			way down, so there is no step where the text clears the picture &mdash;
			the cost is that this section&rsquo;s measure is narrower than the rest of
			the page&rsquo;s.
		</p>

		<header class="page-head">
			<h2 class="as-h1">Creative Work</h2>
			<p class="page-intro">A novel and published poems.</p>
		</header>

		<section class="work">
			<div class="beside">
				<div class="beside-text">
					<h2><em>Flight</em></h2>
					<p class="work-meta">A novel &middot; 80,000 words &middot; Under agent&nbsp;review</p>
					<p>
						<em>Flight</em> is a work of literary fiction about risk and
						resistance, light and dark energies&nbsp;&mdash; and the barriers
						people create to preserve their comfortable, ziplocked lives.
					</p>
					<p>
						Structured in six sections that correspond to spiritual dates and
						martyrs, the novel dramatizes two months in the life of a woman who
						works in an exotic bird store. Her best friend is a circus
						contortionist. She has three love interests: a bashful policeman, an
						egomaniacal astrophysicist, and a distant fianc&eacute;. At the
						center of her story is Maddie, a yellow-collared macaw.
					</p>
					<p>
						It is perhaps the most meaningful project I have completed.
					</p>
				</div>
				<Image
					class="beside-image"
					src={inset}
					alt=""
					widths={[176, 264, 352]}
					sizes="(max-width: 46rem) 34vw, 11rem"
				/>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

	<hr class="mock-rule" />
</Layout>

<style>
	.mock-head {
		padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 4.5rem) 2.5rem;
	}

	.mock-head h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
	}

	.mock-kicker {
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.16em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.mock-intro {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 34rem;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.mock-label {
		margin: 2.5rem 0 0.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.mock-note {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 34rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.84rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.mock-elision {
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.mock-rule {
		border: 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		margin: 3rem 0 0;
	}

	/* From the live Creative Work page, so the measure is the real one. */
	.page-head {
		padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.as-h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1.05;
		letter-spacing: -0.015em;
	}

	.page-intro {
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 0.6vw, 1.3rem);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.work {
		padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.work.no-rule {
		border-top: 0;
	}

	.work h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
	}

	.work h2 em {
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.work-meta {
		margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.work p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.cite-list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.cite-list li {
		padding-block: 0.7rem;
		padding-left: 1.4rem;
		text-indent: -1.4rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.cite-list li + li {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.cite-title {
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}

	/* 1 — beside the page head */
	.page-head.split {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		align-items: start;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.head-portrait {
		width: 12rem;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 2px;
	}

	/* 2 — a band under the page head */
	.photo-band {
		background: var(--color-paper-raised);
		border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
	}

	.band-image {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 2px;
	}

	.band-caption {
		margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	/* 3 — inset beside the poems */
	.measure {
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.inset-image {
		float: right;
		width: 11rem;
		height: auto;
		margin: 0.4rem 0 1.25rem 2rem;
		border-radius: 2px;
	}

	/* 5 — a column beside Flight */
	.beside {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.beside-text p {
		max-width: none;
	}

	.beside-image {
		width: 11rem;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 2px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 46rem) {
		.beside {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}

		.beside-image {
			width: 9rem;
		}

		.page-head.split {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}

		.head-portrait {
			width: 9rem;
			order: -1;
		}

		.inset-image {
			float: none;
			display: block;
			width: 9rem;
			margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		}
	}
</style>
